# Host Console Executable

Use this pattern when creating or changing a console host executable named `<Prefix>.Host.Console`.

## Template Placeholders

Replace placeholders with names from the target solution:

| Placeholder | Example | Role |
|-------------|---------|------|
| `<Prefix>` | `Acme.Product` | Solution/project prefix |
| `HostConfiguration` | typed settings for the host | Main `appsettings` section |
| `FeatureConfiguration` | typed settings for an integration | Secondary `appsettings` section |
| `AddHostConfiguration()` | registration extension on `ContainerBuilder` | Registers `HostConfiguration` |
| `AddHost()` | registration extension on `ContainerBuilder` | Registers production host services |
| `HostCompositionRoot` | static composition class | Wires the production service graph |
| `HostRuntime` | runtime wrapper type | Resolved from DI for composition tests |
| `IApplicationService` | primary domain abstraction | Called by `ConsoleAppLogic` |
| `ApplicationRequest` | domain input model | Built from command-line arguments |
| `IConsoleAppLogic` | console entry contract | Resolved from DI in `Main` |
| `IResultConsoleFormatter` | formatter abstraction | Formats application results for stdout |

## Solution Structure

Host executables sit beside a shared composition library. Each executable has its own unit test project; shared host tests and integration tests live in separate projects.

```
src/
  Prefix.Host/                    # shared composition library (not executable)
    Configuration/
    Composition/
    DependencyInjection/
    Models/
  Prefix.Host.Api/                # Web API executable (see host-api.mdc)
  Prefix.Host.Console/            # console executable
    Program.cs
    appsettings.json
    Infrastructure/
      Abstractions/
      ConsoleAppLogic.cs
      ConsoleAppLogicConfigurationExtensions.cs
      ConsoleAppLogicServiceExtensions.cs
      ConsoleExitCode.cs
      ResultConsoleFormatter.cs
      StandardConsoleOutput.cs
      TextWriterConsoleOutput.cs
  Prefix.Host.test/
  Prefix.Host.Api.test/
  Prefix.Host.Console.test/
  Prefix.Host.test.integration/
```

## Role In The Solution

- The console project is a **thin executable**. It parses command-line input, runs the application workflow, and returns a process exit code.
- Shared composition and `AddHost` registration live in `<Prefix>.Host`.
- The console project references **only** `<Prefix>.Host`. Do not add direct `<ProjectReference>` entries to domain or integration projects.

## Project Layout

- Project name: `<Prefix>.Host.Console`
- Test project name: `<Prefix>.Host.Console.test`
- Sdk: `Microsoft.NET.Sdk` with `<OutputType>Exe</OutputType>`

Do **not** create a `Console/` code folder when the project is already named `*.Host.Console`; that repeats the namespace segment and creates confusing names such as `Prefix.Host.Console.Console`.

```xml
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <UserSecretsId>Prefix-Host-Console</UserSecretsId>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Prefix.Host\Prefix.Host.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <Content Include="appsettings.json">
            <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
        </Content>
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
```

## appsettings.json

Mirror the sections required by `AddConsoleAppLogicConfiguration`:

- `Logging:Files:Path` — consumed by `RegisterLogConfiguration`
- `Host` (or the `HostConfiguration.SectionName` value) — consumed by `AddHostConfiguration`
- `Feature` (or the `FeatureConfiguration.SectionName` value) — consumed by `AddConfiguration<FeatureConfiguration>`

```json
{
  "Logging": {
    "Files": {
      "Path": "%TEMP%\\Prefix.Host.Console\\Logs"
    }
  },
  "Host": {
    "Setting": "value"
  },
  "Feature": {
    "Endpoint": "http://localhost:8080/",
    "Timeout": "00:05:00"
  }
}
```

## Wiring Chain

```
Program.RegisterConfiguration
  └─ RegisterLogConfiguration( "Logging:Files" )
  └─ AddConsoleAppLogicConfiguration()              # in Infrastructure/
       └─ AddHostConfiguration( HostConfiguration.SectionName )
       └─ AddConfiguration<FeatureConfiguration>( FeatureConfiguration.SectionName )

Program.RegisterServices
  └─ AddConsoleAppLogic( configurationProvider )    # in Infrastructure/
       └─ AddHost( configurationProvider )          # in Prefix.Host/DependencyInjection/
       │    └─ resolve HostConfiguration + FeatureConfiguration
       │    └─ HostCompositionRoot.RegisterProductionServices( builder )
       │         └─ external clients, domain services, tools
       │         └─ IApplicationService
       │         └─ HostRuntime
       └─ StandardConsoleOutput as IConsoleOutput
       └─ ResultConsoleFormatter as IResultConsoleFormatter
       └─ ConsoleAppLogic as IConsoleAppLogic

Main
  └─ resolve IConsoleAppLogic
  └─ return await appLogic.RunAsync( args )
       └─ parse args → build ApplicationRequest → IApplicationService.RunAsync
       └─ format result via IResultConsoleFormatter
       └─ write via IConsoleOutput
       └─ return (int)ConsoleExitCode
```

- `Program` registers logging bootstrap only. All other configuration and service wiring lives in `Infrastructure/` extensions.
- `AddConsoleAppLogic` must call `AddHost` before registering console-specific services so `IApplicationService` and configuration are available to `ConsoleAppLogic`.

## Program Bootstrap

- Follow `.cursor/rules/entry-points.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/host-composition.mdc`.
- Use an explicit `Program` class with a **public** `async Task<int> Main`, `RegisterConfiguration`, and `RegisterServices`.
- Use `Host.CreateApplicationBuilder( args )` and `ConfigureDefaultHostApplication<Program>`.
- Pass an empty web-services delegate: `_ => { }`.
- After build, resolve `IConsoleAppLogic` from Autofac and return its exit code.
- On startup failure, log and return `(int)ConsoleExitCode.UnexpectedError`.

```csharp
public static async Task<int> Main( string[] args )
{
    ILogger? logger = null;

    try
    {
        var builder = Host.CreateApplicationBuilder( args );

        builder.ConfigureDefaultHostApplication<Program>(
            string.Empty,
            RegisterConfiguration,
            RegisterServices,
            _ => { } );

        using var host = builder.Build();

        var container = host.Services.GetAutofacRoot();
        logger = container.Resolve<ILogger<Program>>();

        var appLogic = container.Resolve<IConsoleAppLogic>();

        return await appLogic.RunAsync( args );
    }
    catch( Exception ex )
    {
        logger?.LogError( ex, "An error occurred while starting the application" );
        return (int)ConsoleExitCode.UnexpectedError;
    }
}

public static void RegisterConfiguration( ContainerBuilder builder )
{
    builder.RegisterLogConfiguration( "Logging:Files" );
    builder.AddConsoleAppLogicConfiguration();
}

public static void RegisterServices( ContainerBuilder builder,
                                     IAutofacConfigurationProvider configurationProvider )
    => builder.AddConsoleAppLogic( configurationProvider );
```

## Infrastructure Pattern

Colocate console feature wiring beside the console workflow.

| File | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `Infrastructure/Abstractions/IConsoleAppLogic.cs` | Console entry contract (`RunAsync` returns exit code) |
| `Infrastructure/Abstractions/IConsoleOutput.cs` | Console output abstraction for production and tests |
| `Infrastructure/Abstractions/IResultConsoleFormatter.cs` | Human-readable result formatting contract |
| `Infrastructure/ConsoleAppLogic.cs` | Parse args, build `ApplicationRequest`, call `IApplicationService`, format/write output, return exit code |
| `Infrastructure/ConsoleExitCode.cs` | Process exit codes as an `enum`, not `public const int` |
| `Infrastructure/ConsoleAppLogicConfigurationExtensions.cs` | `AddConsoleAppLogicConfiguration()` |
| `Infrastructure/ConsoleAppLogicServiceExtensions.cs` | `AddConsoleAppLogic()` |
| `Infrastructure/StandardConsoleOutput.cs` | Production `IConsoleOutput` |
| `Infrastructure/TextWriterConsoleOutput.cs` | Test `IConsoleOutput` over `TextWriter` |
| `Infrastructure/ResultConsoleFormatter.cs` | Production formatter implementation |

### Configuration extension

```csharp
public static ContainerBuilder AddConsoleAppLogicConfiguration( this ContainerBuilder builder )
{
    builder.AddHostConfiguration( HostConfiguration.SectionName );
    builder.AddConfiguration<FeatureConfiguration>( FeatureConfiguration.SectionName );
    return builder;
}
```

### Service extension

```csharp
public static ContainerBuilder AddConsoleAppLogic( this ContainerBuilder builder,
                                                   IAutofacConfigurationProvider configurationProvider )
{
    builder.AddHost( configurationProvider );

    builder.RegisterType<StandardConsoleOutput>()
           .As<IConsoleOutput>()
           .SingleInstance();

    builder.RegisterType<ResultConsoleFormatter>()
           .As<IResultConsoleFormatter>()
           .SingleInstance();

    builder.RegisterType<ConsoleAppLogic>()
           .As<IConsoleAppLogic>()
           .SingleInstance();

    return builder;
}
```

Registration rules:

- Call `AddHost( configurationProvider )` from the console service extension, not from `Program`.
- Register every console implementation with `.As<IAbstraction>()` and `.SingleInstance()` where appropriate.

## Exit Codes

- Define exit codes in a `ConsoleExitCode` enum: `Success = 0`, `InvalidInput = 1`, `ApplicationFailed = 2`, `UnexpectedError = 3`.
- Return enum values cast to `int` from `IConsoleAppLogic.RunAsync`.
- Map unexpected startup exceptions in `Main` to `ConsoleExitCode.UnexpectedError`.

## Forbidden

- Top-level statements.
- Delegating `Main` to a separate startup class.
- `InternalsVisibleTo` for test assemblies.
- A `Console/` folder inside a `*.Host.Console` project.
- Duplicating production composition that already belongs in `<Prefix>.Host`.
- Executable-specific tests in `<Prefix>.Host.test`; use `<Prefix>.Host.Console.test` instead.

## Tests

Test project layout:

```
Prefix.Host.Console.test/
  Configuration/
    ProgramConfigurationRegistrationTests.cs
    ProgramServiceRegistrationTests.cs
  Infrastructure/
    ConsoleAppLogicTests.cs
    ResultConsoleFormatterTests.cs
```

Required composition tests:

- `ProgramConfigurationRegistrationTests` — call `Program.RegisterConfiguration`, resolve `HostConfiguration` and `FeatureConfiguration`, assert with `BeEquivalentTo`.
- `ProgramServiceRegistrationTests` — build `AutofacConfigurationProvider` with `Program.RegisterConfiguration`, call `AddConfigurationProvider`, register `NullLogger<>` as `ILogger<>`, call `Program.RegisterServices`, resolve `IConsoleAppLogic`, `HostRuntime`, `IApplicationService`, `IResultConsoleFormatter`, `IConsoleOutput`, verify types and that the runtime exposes the same application service instance, assert configuration values.

Feature tests:

- Test `ConsoleAppLogic` with mocked `IApplicationService`, `IConsoleOutput`, and formatter dependencies.
- Use `TextWriterConsoleOutput` in tests that need captured console output.
- End-to-end console scenarios that call real external services belong in `<Prefix>.Host.test.integration`.

Build test configuration with `AddJsonString()`, not `AddInMemoryCollection()`.
